        <body>
            <div xml:id="d268">

                <pb facs="0416" n="369" xml:id="pg369"/>

                <head>268. Telegram 834 to Geneva<anchor n="1" xml:id="d268-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1955-10-06">October 6, 1955, 5:35
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <pb facs="d268-1" n="1" type="facsimile" xml:id="d268-1"/>
                <p>834. For Johnson.</p>
                <p>Penultimate paragraph Department’s 826.</p>
                <p>Father McGuire of NCWC advises Belgian priest’s report not based on recent
                    contact with Walsh. Walsh’s superior sent him telegram September 23 instructing
                    him leave Red China and report travel plans soonest. Although no word yet from
                    Walsh, McGuire assures us Walsh will comply these instructions.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#bold">Dulles</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
